---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Harbor Legal Independent Index" activeNav="home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">MVP - Public preview</p>
      <h1>Tracking legal source activity across America.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Harbor Legal Independent Index tracks legislative sources across federal and state systems,
        monitors bill movement and source reliability, and publishes trend reports on where legal
        activity is changing. Court content is not the main product surface, except for circuit
        courts and above where it materially changes the legal landscape.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/search/">Explore source search</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/reports/">Read the latest report</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/method/">How we count</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">What we track</div>
          <div class="card-value">Legal sources</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Federal and state bill pages, search portals, feeds, and official endpoint surfaces -
            broken out by jurisdiction, chamber, topic, and stage coverage.
          </p>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/search/">Open search page</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">What we track</div>
          <div class="card-value">Bills first</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            The core focus is laws and legislation. Case law is only a later layer, limited to
            federal circuit courts, state supreme courts, and the Supreme Court.
          </p>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/method/">See scope rules</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">What we publish</div>
          <div class="card-value">Monitoring plans</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Trend reports, source-health views, and endpoint coverage maps that show which federal
            and state systems are stable, changing, blocked, or worth deeper extraction work.
          </p>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/reports/">View report examples</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What changes</p>
          <h2>The kind of source and trend signals we surface</h2>
        </div>
        <a href="/search/">Search coverage -&gt;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="surface">
        <div class="signal-stack">
          <div class="signal-item">A state legislature changed its bill search markup and the scraper drift detector caught it before collection fully failed.</div>
          <div class="signal-item">A federal source exposed a stable JSON feed, letting us replace brittle HTML scraping with a cheaper direct collector.</div>
          <div class="signal-item">A source started rate-limiting basic fetches, so it moved into a fallback browser or Bright Data lane instead of blocking the whole pipeline.</div>
          <div class="signal-item">Bill stage coverage expanded from introduced-only to committee, chamber passage, and enactment once the endpoint map stabilized.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Roadmap</p>
          <h2>Where the product is headed</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="roadmap-grid">
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Stage one</div>
          <h3>Search and source coverage</h3>
          <p>Build a searchable map of federal and state legal sources, endpoint types, scraper status, and drift risk.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Stage two</div>
          <h3>Trend and monitoring views</h3>
          <p>Turn collection into timelines, coverage gaps, source-health alerts, and topic-level bill movement dashboards.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Stage three</div>
          <h3>Higher-court signal layer</h3>
          <p>Add circuit courts and above only where decisions materially reshape the legal landscape behind legislative topics.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Stage four</div>
          <h3>Membership and saved workflows</h3>
          <p>Later, gated accounts can unlock saved searches, alerts, source watchlists, and paid access to refined analytics.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
